ay picks, Jill does. So, you can check that out. It`s on the June issue but it`s on stands right now.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: OK. Hoda, over to you.\par \par \uc2 MARTIN: Thank you, darling. Just ahead, we got the founder of Scott`s Cheap Flights right here to help you find affordable fares for your summer vacations. But first, this is Today on NBC.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: We are back with our new series. It`s all about ways you can save money this summer. We`re going to start with your summer vacation.\par \par \uc2 So, despite soaring inflation, the record gas prices, you still can get a get away without breaking the bank. We`ve got just the person to tell us how. His name is \uc2 Scott Keyes\uc2 . He`s the founder of Scott`s Cheap Flights. He`s here for the first time on Today. He`s got tips and tricks for scoring cheap flights.\par \par \uc2 Hey, Scott, welcome. I feel like our headlines for the last week and more, have been gas prices are high. It`s tough to get rental cars, hotels, et cetera. So, people planning a vacation might be going, oh my gosh, like how do I even start? So, if you are looking at somewhere and saying when is the best time for me to plan a vacation? What time would you would you pick?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT KEYES\uc2 , FOUNDER, SCOTT`S CHEAP FLIGHTS: Think about it like your gym resolution, the best time to have started would have been six months ago and the second best time to start is today.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: OK.\par \par \uc2 KEYES: Same with booking those summer flights. It would have been cheaper if you booked it over the winter, but you don`t want to put it off until the last minute because fares tend to actually skyrocket if you wait to the last minute. They don`t tend to come down in price. So try to get it booked sooner rather than later. And there are still some summer flight sales available, but you need to book them quickly.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: That`s interesting what you said about don`t wait last minute, because I thought, well, like airlines just want to fill the seats at the end. So if I just wait maybe I`ll find a good seat.\par \par \uc2 KEYES: That would make sense, wouldn`t it? But what the airlines think is that, look, the folks who tend to book their flights last minute aren`t leisure travelers, they`re not vacationers like you and I. It`s business travelers who will pay top dollar because it`s their company paying not them.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: OK. So, if I want to book a flight and I want an inexpensive flight, what place do you think is the best value?\par \par \uc2 KEYES: I`m going to throw a curveball at you here, Hoda. The cheapest deals and the best value deals for this summer are actually to Europe. You know, everybody wants to travel this summer but where you see the most demand is domestically. But the airlines actually don`t have enough flights domestically, still down about 15%, but flights to Europe, fully rebounded from where it was pre-pandemic. But the actual demand for them still down 20%, 30%.\par \par \uc2 [08:55:02]\par \par \uc2 This is why you see flights still available in New York to Oslo for $242 round trip or New York to Rome demand for them still down 20 30% This is why you see flights still available in New York to Oslo for 242 round trip Oh, or New York to Rome for 446 round trip for this summer still available.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: So if you`re looking for flights, people don`t -- I mean, some people go right to the airlines, some people go to one of those in between things like \uc2 Expedia\uc2  or whatever. What do you think is the best way to find the best deal if you`re booking a flight?\par \par \uc2 KEYES: So the open secret is actually, it doesn`t make a ton of difference where you search for your flight. I do recommend searching on one of the comparison sites, you know, there`s Google Flights, \uc2 Expedia\uc2 , \uc2 Orbitz\uc2 , whichever one you prefer and you find the most the best for your taste go for it. But you do want to book directly with the airline, generally, because you get certain protections under federal law when you book directly.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: So, when you`re booking, you know, it tells you like this time mattered, does price matter, you know. What should you focus on if you want to try to get the best deal?\par \par \uc2 KEYES: My best recommendation is, look, if you`re going to -- if you`re really hoping to get a cheap flight, take the normal three step process that you use to search for flights and flip it on its head. The normal way we searched, we decide where we want to go, when we want to go, and then we look at price. And we just hope and pray for a cheap flight. Instead, if cheap flights are priority, don`t make them the last priority, make them the top priority.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: So go with price first --\par \par \uc2 KEYES: Go with price first.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: -- and then see, oh, you could go here, here or here.\par \par \uc2 KEYES: Exactly. Do you want to go to Rome? Do you want to go to Oslo? And then go from there.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Hey, by the way, very great first run on Today Show.\par \par \uc2 KEYES: I`m so honored to be here.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: A lot of great ideas, happy that you`re here. Great ideas. Just ahead on Hoda and Jenna, we`re catching up with Idina Menzel. But first, our 3rd Hour gang and --\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2022 NBCUniversal.  ALL RIGHTS   RESERVED. Transcription Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TODA000020220520ei5k000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News\par