.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: We`re going to do our best.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: All right. So, let`s get started. First of all, you`ve got simple do`s and don`ts when it comes to home decor.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: Right. So -- yes. You know, a lot of people have been buying houses. It`s just been crazy. They move from apartment. They get bigger houses, what have you. They come in and they`re like, OK. I got to do it all at once.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: And, you know, where I do start? Where do I finish? And yada, yada. And it just becomes chaotic and hectic. And so, I recommend, starting with the place that you need the most, that you love the most. So, that`s the kitchen, it`s the family room, maybe it`s the bedrooms. But start there and then, go from that. Otherwise, you are just going to do a half job on everything.\par \par \uc2 JONES: You`re right.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: And it`s just never going to get done.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Nice catch there.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: Yes, yes. Very good catch. I know.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Almost right there. Almost right there. Very good.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Let`s talk about this first set up here. It`s funny. I`m in this phase and we`re going to \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and all these homes look so pretty.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: I know.\par \par \uc2 JONES: And all decorated --\par \par \uc2 DREYER: And you just want to buy everything.\par \par \uc2 JONES: And all is like cream and linen and beautiful and there are no toys anywhere. So, is this that?\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: This is sleek. This is cool. Well, what happens is people they move and they bring their furniture with them and the furniture doesn`t necessarily fit with their new space.\par \par \uc2 JONES: OK.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: It is too big. It`s too small. It just looks out of place. So, my recommendation is look for furniture, you know, find furniture that fit yours new space.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Wait a minute. This one grabbed my attention. I thought if you have a big family, you would want the oversized sofa.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: OK. Sometimes, yes. And so that -- you know, some -- a little asterisk right there.\par \par \uc2 JONES: OK.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: OK.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: And maybe in the family room, in like TV room, yes. But like in your living room where you are going to be entertaining, it is nice to have separate spaces where you can have conversations.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Seating areas.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: So, it is not just one big couch taking up the entire space.\par \par \uc2 JONES: OK.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: OK. Let`s talk about lighting over here.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: OK.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: Because I feel like lighting is one of those things where you need layers to make it look bright.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: 100 percent. I mean, ideally you have as many different layers of light as possible. Floor lights, table lights, ceiling lights, sconces. If you can`t have a lot of different lights, make sure you have at least dimmers on your lights because you want set different moods.\par \par \uc2 LLAMAS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: You don`t want the same like light all the time.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: OK.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: And then, what about bulbs? I mean, you talk about soft white bulbs. And a lot of people are trying to be, you know, conscious.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: Ecofriendly.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Ecofriendly. LEDs, have they made big changes?\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: LEDs have come so far. And they are energy efficient. So, that is going to be a nice on your power bill. And two, yes, you can now dim LED bubs. You get the warmer light. Actually, what`s really cool about LED bulbs now is you can change the temperature from daylight all the way down to like that old school incandescent warm yellow.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Different colors?\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: You can change the color temperature, exactly. And there`s really just a button.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: But how do you make it not flicker when you`re on the lowest dim setting? It drives me crazy because I want the light lower but it is like flickering.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: Right. So, it`s about getting the right bulb, getting the right LED bulb. Not -- you know, some of the older bulbs don`t dim as well as some of the newer bulbs.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: OK.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: So, it`s really about getting the right bulb for your light.\par \par \uc2 JONES: OK.\par \par \uc2 LLAMAS: You know, George, you walk into so many homes now and people are going minimalist or going plain, white, black, grays. I know you have some Miami roots. Sometimes you want to come in, you just want to hit with some color, you know.\par \par \uc2 [09:45:00]\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: This argue -- this is my wife and I, this conversation.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: I`m the guy who wants to bring all the color. She`s like, well, reel it back a little bit and let kind of these pieces pop. So, whether it is art work, your pillows, your rugs, your furniture. Sometimes people just throw all the color on the walls and then, that mutes out everything else.\par \par \uc2 JONES: True.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: It is nice to go with a neutral on your walls. Again, I fought this. My wife painted the back -- our back wall in our bedroom black and it makes everything else in the bedroom pop.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Pop.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: Oh, wow.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: So, yes, when you take away color it allows the other colors to really be the star of the show.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: And you can do instrumental theater in there too.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: You can do a little instrumental. Come on in. Black box.\par \par \uc2 LLAMAS: Was she sending you a message? No, I don`t know. OK.\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Don`t ignore a ceiling?\par \par \uc2 OLIPHANT: Don`t ignore -- yes, it`s the fifth wall. People like --\par