nd on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Well, coming up, we`re going to have a festive dessert that you are going to want to add to your Easter menu.\par \par \uc2 And then, tomorrow on the "3rd Hour of TODAY," I`m so excited for this one, fresh off his Grammy win for album of the year, our buddy, Jon Batiste is joining us live in studio. "3rd Hour of TODAY" will be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [09:50:00]\par \par \uc2 DREYER: Well, Easter Sunday is right around the corner. And this morning, on "TODAY Food," we are baking a tasty treat that all your peeps are sure to love.\par \par \uc2 LLAMAS: I like that.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Cookbook author and foodie in New York vlogger Vallery Lomas is here to show us how to make a pecan Bundt cake.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: Oh, pecan.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Perfect for any celebration. Or pecan. The recipe is from her newest cook book "Life is What You Bake It."\par \par \uc2 Vallery, good morning.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Good morning.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Thanks for being here.\par \par \uc2 VALLERY LOMAS, COOKBOOK AUTHOR: Thanks, guys.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: OK. So, you are making this Bundt cake.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: It`s really flour.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: First of all, what kind do we use? And how -- when we scoop it, you know, sometimes we over scoop.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: Exactly. So, we`re using all-purpose flour. And so, the way that you scoop so that you get the right measurement, and it is not too caked in there, so you get a sense dense cake is you do what`s call scoop and level. So, I`ve just got a spoon.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: Light and fluffy.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Like I`m back in home ed.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: I know.\par \par \uc2 JONES: What happens if you use too much flour?\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: It will be dense. So, I`m just, you know, using a straight edge to level it. I`m using an angled spatula but you can use a butter knife.\par \