oking for?\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: Right. We`re looking for light and fluffy.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: OK.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: OK.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: So, while that is going, we can go ahead and add our eggs.\par \par \uc2 JONES: OK.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: So, we`re just going to add our eggs one at a time. And by adding them one at a time, what that is going to do is it is going to make it so we`re not adding too much liquid all at once and our batter just has a chance to --\par \par \uc2 DREYER: OK.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: What is the trick to adding the dry ingredients?\par \par \uc2 DREYER: All at once.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: Right. The trick is to turn off the mixer so it doesn`t get everywhere.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: Right.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: But yes. So, we can go ahead and we need to add the rest of our eggs but we`ll --\par \par \uc2 DREYER: Right.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: We`ll pretend we`ve done that because we don`t want to run out of time.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: I see we have some --\par \par \uc2 JONES: We don`t have any left.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: So, we`ve got toasted pecans. And what I`m going to do, I`m going to --\par \par \uc2 ROKER: You said pecans.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: Yes. I said -- I`m from Louisiana. I say pecans.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: OK.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: And I`m just going to roughly chop them because I like when you bite into the cake, you have like a nice big bite.\par \par \uc2 JONES: A big crunch.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: Exactly. And because they are toasted, you get umami flavor that balances out the sweetness.\par \par \uc2 DREYER: OK.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: So, what goes in this?\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: So, we`re adding our pecans.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Right.\par \par \uc2 JONES: OK.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: We`ve got our crushed pineapple. That is going to make this really moist. And I`ve got some golden raisins.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Nice.\par \par \uc2 LOMAS: Do you want to help me maybe mix this altogether?\par \par \uc2 JONES: Yum.\par \par \uc2 LLAMA