ER: We`re back now. And Jacob you`ve got the PopStart this morning.\par \par \uc2 SOBOROFF: It`s going to be a good one. Coming up, we`re going to go Gotham as we get a new look at the upcoming Batman movie with Robert Pattinson and Zoe Kravitz as Catwoman. But first your local news.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [07:56:12]\par \par \uc2 LATOYIA EDWARDS, NBC10 BOSTON ANCHOR: Wishing you a great start to your day, 7:56. I`m Latoyia Edwards. Thank you so much for starting your morning with us here at NBC in Boston. Well, some freezing rain to start the morning just some clouds right now. We check in with chief meteorologist Matt Noyes in your First Alert forecast.\par \par \uc2 NOYES: You know what, it was a little tricky in some spots this morning back roads in particular, right. But most of the treated roads held up OK and now today we`re going into the 40s. We`ll do it with some splashes of sunshine. We could push 50 if you`re south of town. Then as we get to the evening and overnight between 9:00 and 10:00 p.m., some light rain and snow showers come through. But look at this, by this time tomorrow, they`re long gone. What do you get out of it? You probably get a little trace of some snow or ice during the overnight.\par \par \uc2 I think for the most part the roads with the treatment they have on them still are going to end up being fine. Tomorrow, it is a little bit cooler, but you`re still around 40. In fact, you`re 40 or better through the end of the week. New Year`s Eve rain on the way, but I`m thinking if the timing holds as it looks right now, we`ll come in till after midnight. That would be nice. It will rain New Year`s Day and could end as snow later on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 EDWARDS: It would be nice Matt. Today, the man charged in connection to a Woburn mother`s death will appear in court. Bruce Maiben was arrested one day after Sherelle Pringle`s family found her dead in Saugus days after she was reported missing. He`s being held without