r other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 [19:20:00] LESTER HOLT: As you know, the holiday shopping season is here. But this year, businesses both big and small, are feeling the squeeze. In an NBC News exclusive, \uc2 Jo Ling Kent\uc2  spoke to the U.S. Labor Secretary about when we`ll see relief in the economic threat from the new Omicron variant.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 JO LING KENT\uc2 , NBC NEWS BUSINESS AND TECHNOLOGY CORRESPONDENT: For the first time, Labor Secretary Marty Walsh visiting the clogged \uc2 Port of Los Angeles\uc2  filled with idling container ships.\par \par \uc2 MARTY WALSH, U.S. SECRETARY OF LABOR: I would say that the ports might not be operating 24/7 but they`re certainly operating at higher capacity.\par \par \uc2 KENT: When do you think the supply chain will get back to normal?\par \par \uc2 WALSH: I don`t think there`s ever a normal in the supply chain. I think it`s always been, you know, ups and downs.\par \par \uc2 KENT: The Port of LA says the number of containers waiting to be unloaded has dropped 37 percent since late October. But Fed Chief Jerome Powell today laying out new fears brought on by the Omicron variant.\par \par \uc2 POWELL: Greater concerns about the virus could reduce people`s willingness to work in person, which would slow progress in the labor market and intensify supply chain disruptions.\par \par \uc2 KENT: How are you as labor secretary going to incentivize people to keep going back to work?\par \par \uc2 WALSH: I think the biggest thing is as we figure out the new variant, we just need to continue to stress people getting vaccinated, getting boosted, wearing masks, being careful.\par \par \uc2 KENT: But it`s more than that. For small business owner Keewa Nurullah, hiring at her Chicago boutique Kido is very expensive because she has to compete for workers with major retailers.\par \par \uc2 KEEWA NURULLAH, OWNER, KIDO: Unfortunately, if we are short-staffed, that affects everything.\par \par \uc2 KENT: On top of that, she`s only been able to get 60 percent of what she needs to stock her shelves this holiday season.\par \par \uc2 NURULLAH: We have at least a dozen of our best sellers that we`ve always leaned on during this time just haven`t been available.\par \par \uc2 KENT: How do you make sure that small businesses are properly served in this pandemic when they try to get their stuff in for holiday season?\par \par \uc2 WALSH: I think when we look at the unloading and delivery of goods and services to our country, of goods to our country, I don`t look into the lens of the big companies and then the small companies. I look to everybody`s company at the same time.\par \par \uc2 KENT: Companies large and small desperate for supply chain solutions. \uc2 Jo Ling Kent\uc2 , NBC News, Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HOLT: And up next, on Giving Tuesday, we`ll introduce you to a remarkable art program that helps people stay out of prison now struggling for support.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2021 NBCUniversal.  ALL RIGHTS   RESERVED. Transcription Copyright 2021 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may  not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of  the content. \par \par \uc2 Document NTLN000020211201ehbu000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 TODAY WITH HODA & JENNA for November 11, 2021, NBC\b0\par\par\uc2 Hoda Kotb, Jenna Bush Hager \par \uc2 8,060 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 November 2021\par \uc2 NBC News: Today\par \uc2 TODA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2021 NBCUniversal. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Transcription Copyright 2021 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All