ank God. One person that knows the song but even with a -- with a number one hit, I was playing places that didn`t even have a stage.\par \par \uc2 So, to compare it to the that, I mean, it`s -- there is no comparison.\par \par \uc2 We can reach the stars.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Blake`s latest single We Can Reach the Stars is his most sentimental one yet.\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: You know, Gwen is -- she`s been pretty hard on me the last few years as far as -- she doesn`t think I don`t write enough music, so I thought you know what, I`m going to take this opportunity to write a song for her as my vows.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I`m just reading the lyrics and it feels like some sort of love poem. We always said we wish we`d met long before we finally did. But ever since that first kiss, I mean, it`s just so romantic.\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: Well --\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Are you blushing -- are you blushing?\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: Actually, yesterday -- I am blushing a little bit. Yesterday, I was driving to work and I played the song. And I remember thinking, wow, I did it. I wrote a song for my wife. No one can ever take that away. Anytime we get our whatever, I`ll just put that on in the background.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: It`s pretty romantic. OK, let`s talk about The Voice. Ariana Grande calls you granddaddy, is that right? Granddad.\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: It is true. You know, it started out as like just a dad. And as if that wasn`t painful enough. That`s turned into granddad.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: And the thing is, what`s your comeback? You just call her granddaughter?\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: If you look at Arianna, it`s hard to pick her apart. I mean, she`s Ariana Grande. What? There are no flaws.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: You`ve been posting some pictures on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: I have.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I`m just wondering, did this person think he was going to marry Gwen Stefani?\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: Of course, I did. I mean, look at that hairdo. There was no resisting those locks.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: What about this look? Is this something you could ever grow -- could you grow your hair this long again?\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: It`s not only is that painful to look at, it`s painful the process of growing your hair.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: We have some other ones but frankly, you were just cute.\par \par \uc2 While I loved looking at throwback pics, we couldn`t wrap without a Hoda & Jenna quiz.\par \par \uc2 Are you ready?\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: All right, bring it on.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK, best wedding gift you received.\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: We had an entire church pew that was given to us and everybody -- there weren`t that many people. I think there was about 30 people at our wedding. Everybody signed it and wrote a message on it. Now, that pew is in the chapel. That`s pretty, pretty special to she and I both.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: How many pair of cowboy boots do you own?\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: I own a probably about 10 pair but they`re all the exact same boot?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Your favorite hair color of your wife`s?\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: There`s a lot of choices in there. There`s been a few times where she`s kind of done a Marilyn Monroe look with her hair and oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: that`s good stuff.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Thank you so much, Blake. We`ll send you some of these pictures.\par \par \uc2 SHELTON: Oh, please. Oh, yes. I`d love to have those so I can shred them.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Sweet.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Oh, just sharing just some one-on-one time.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: You know what --\par \par \uc2 HAGER: One on one time, in fact, that`s probably where I lost my voice. I just couldn`t stop chuckling with him.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: He`s adorable.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Right? I know. Well, he did ask about you.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: When? Not for five seconds.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: That poster is heade